WEBVTT

NOTE Timing is estimated from script and acoustic pauses; listening review pending.

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.325
Valentina now knows the decision:
approve a split launch today.

00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:09.886
Next, she needs enough structure to
make the message complete without

00:00:09.886 --> 00:00:14.674
turning it into a report. DECIDE
is a planning method, not a

00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:19.883
six-section template. D is
Decision: what must be decided or

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:25.102
accomplished? E is Executive
headline: if the audience reads

00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:27.365
one sentence, what must they know?

00:00:27.365 --> 00:00:32.789
C is Critical evidence: which
one or two facts support

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:36.774
the conclusion? I is Impact: what
changes for the customer or the

00:00:36.774 --> 00:00:40.810
business? D is Direction:
what do you recommend?

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:44.495
E is Execution: who
does what, and by when?

00:00:44.495 --> 00:00:45.795
You answer all six before writing.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:50.440
The final message may be
only three or four sentences.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.140
Structure does not
make a message longer.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.720
It makes every sentence earn its place.
